---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import WorkedExample from '../../components/WorkedExample.astro';
---
<Page
  title="Rules"
  description="In ArborSpace the rule is the unit of value: expert knowledge written down explicitly, applied by the system, readable by anyone."
  eyebrow="Product · Rules"
  heading="The rule is the unit of value."
  lead="A piece of expert knowledge written down explicitly, which the system applies and anyone can review."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Declarative and inspectable</h2>
        <p>
          Rules are declarative: they state a condition and a conclusion, nothing hidden. Every
          conclusion traces back to a named rule and an explicit path of relationships.
        </p>
        <p>
          Rules run against the data, and a similarity engine matches each case with the firm’s
          previous ones.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Written with your experts</h2>
        <p>
          In a pilot, the first fifteen rules are written in two weeks, starting from three
          questions put to your experts.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/resources/pilot">How the pilot works →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap"><WorkedExample /></div>
  </section>
</Page>
